# tools/css/check-webref-package.py: the places where the tables (generated from the pinned w3c/webref data) and the @webref/css package
# (tools/css/WEBREF_PACKAGE) do not say the same thing about a name or its syntax. Columns: kind, name, reason (at least twenty characters,
# and true: each reason says what was looked at). A difference that is not here fails, and so does a row for a difference that is gone.
#
# Two kinds of difference are here.
#
# * type: a name one reading has and the other does not. (The tables read the types and functions the pin nests inside a type, an at-rule,
#   a descriptor or a selector, and the check compares them with the package's: 37 of them were not read until the check found it, see
#   tools/css/webref_model.py `nested_definitions`.)
# * type-syntax: both have the name and the texts differ; the reason gives both and says which side is the older reading.
#
type	output-value	the pin nests <output-value> in calc-interpolate(), color-interpolate(), interpolate() and transform-interpolate() with no grammar of its own (the entries carry only keyword values, so it is prose); the package lists no such type
